| Volume-trend continuation | 1d | 0.01335 | Not admissible under required convention | 1,449 | 8.92 | Failed admission |
| Range-efficiency trend | 1d | -0.00153 | Negative | 1,775 | 14.57 | Failed |
| Range-efficiency trend | 5d | 0.01311 | Not sufficiently robust | 1,771 | 14.57 | Failed |
| Range-efficiency trend | 10d | 0.03415 | Not sufficiently robust | 1,766 | 14.57 | Failed |

The benchmark admission thresholds are absolute daily IC ≥ 0.0070 and absolute daily ICIR ≥ 0.0840. The VIX-conditioned reversal passed with broad coverage and positive annual-regime results. However, it is highly correlated with the existing plain reversal signal, with reported pooled correlation of approximately 0.92, so it should be treated as a regime-sensitive refinement rather than independent alpha.

